        "scope": "in_scope",
        "statement": "Let $\\mathbb K=\\R$ or $\\C$, let $1\\le k$, $1\\le r$, and $k+r\\le n$.\nLet $z_1,\\ldots,z_r$ be orthonormal, set\n$V=\\operatorname{span}(z_1,\\ldots,z_r)^\\perp$, and take any\n$u\\in\\Lambda^k V$, not necessarily decomposable. Put\n$b=z_r\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge z_1\\wedge u$.\nFor every real array $(a_S)_{S\\in\\binom{[n]}k}$,\n\\begin{equation}\n \\sum_{T\\in\\binom{[n]}{k+r}}\\left(\\min_{\\substack{S\\subset T\\\\|S|=k}}a_S\\right)|b_T|^2\n \\ \\le\\ \\sum_{S\\in\\binom{[n]}k}a_S|u_S|^2\n \\ \\le\\ \\sum_{T\\in\\binom{[n]}{k+r}}\\left(\\max_{\\substack{S\\subset T\\\\|S|=k}}a_S\\right)|b_T|^2.\n\\end{equation}",
        "status": "preparing",
